-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. two-traces.l4 with the ledger-reading rule two hops
-- away: this file imports hop-b.l4 only, whose `shop is closed` is `taken now`
-- of taken.l4. Each #TRACE must read it afresh through both hops: the first
-- trace (peek) gives two COMMITs and WITHIN 10, the second (skip) one COMMIT
-- and WITHIN 9, as each does alone.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hop-b`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `shop is closed`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `shop is closed` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
